.\" Adapted for BNU from the GNU Coreutils 9.11 manual page; see doc/README.md.
.TH MKFIFO "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
mkfifo \- make FIFOs (named pipes)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfifo
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,NAME\/\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Create named pipes (FIFOs) with the given NAMEs.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo-m'\fB\-m, \-\-mode=\,MODE\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
set file permission bits to MODE, not a=rw \- umask
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo-Z'\fB\-Z\fP\X'tty: link'
set the SELinux security context to default type
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo--context'\fB\-\-context[=CTX]\fP\X'tty: link'
like \fB\-Z\fR, or if CTX is specified then set the
SELinux or SMACK security context to CTX
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mkfifo#mkfifo--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mkfifo#mkfifo--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
